---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const pageTitle = "Microcredentials";
---
<BaseLayout pageTitle={pageTitle}>
    <div style="background-color: #1B3054; min-height: 100vh; padding: 2rem;">
        <div class="header-line">
            <h1>Microcredentials</h1>
        </div>

        <section class="intro-section">
            <p>Microcredentials are digital badges used to help match employers and graduate schools with candidates who have achieved a set of well-defined skills, competencies and strengths within a field of study. These badges, when included on application portals like Indeed and LinkedIn, help job and graduate school applicants rise through an algorithmically parsed applicant pool in ways that a degree alone might not. Each microcredential consists of a small number of credit-bearing courses (typically three) specifically packaged together to highlight the skill or competency students will gain. In many cases, students may earn these badges through completing coursework that can also fulfill requirements of their academic major and minor programs. Specific Microcredentials offered through the Computer Science Program are listed below.</p>

            <div class="accordion-section">
                <h2>Available Microcredentials</h2>
                <div class="accordion-list">
                    <details>
                        <summary>AI-Driven Content Creation</summary>
                    </details>
                    <details>
                        <summary>Content Creation (in collaboration with Art)</summary>
                    </details>
                    <details>
                        <summary>Artificial Intelligence Engineering</summary>
                    </details>
                    <details>
                        <summary>Cybersecurity Risk Analysis</summary>
                    </details>
                    <details>
                        <summary>Data Analysis with Python and R</summary>
                    </details>
                    <details>
                        <summary>Data-driven Health Informatics</summary>
                    </details>
                    <details>
                        <summary>Embedded Systems Engineering</summary>
                    </details>
                    <details>
                        <summary>Game Design</summary>
                    </details>
                    <details>
                        <summary>Product Development in the Internet of Things</summary>
                    </details>
                    <details>
                        <summary>Programming with Web Technologies</summary>
                    </details>
                    <details>
                        <summary>Site Reliability Engineering</summary>
                    </details>
                    <details>
                        <summary>Software Development with Python</summary>
                    </details>
                    <details>
                        <summary>Software Performance Engineering</summary>
                    </details>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>
    </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
    h1 {
        font-family: 'Bebas Neue', sans-serif;
        font-size: 64px;
        color: #FEDA48;
        margin-bottom: -0.25rem;
        line-height: 1;
    }

    .intro-section {
        color: #F5F7FA;
        line-height: 1.7;
        max-width: 100%;
    }

    .intro-section p {
        margin-top: 0;
    }

    .accordion-section {
        margin-top: 2rem;
        width: 100%;
    }

    .accordion-section h2 {
        font-size: 32px;
        color: #FEDA48;
        margin-bottom: 1rem;
    }

    .accordion-list {
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;
        gap: 0.75rem;
        width: 100%;
    }

    details {
        background-color: #1B3054;
        border: 2px solid #FFFFFF;
        border-radius: 0;
        padding: 0.85rem 1rem;
        box-shadow: none;
    }

    summary {
        font-family: 'Bebas Neue', sans-serif;
        cursor: pointer;
        color: #FFFFFF;
        font-size: 20px;
        font-weight: 600;
        list-style: none;
        display: flex;
        align-items: center;
        justify-content: space-between;
        gap: 1rem;
    }

    summary::after {
        content: '⌄';
        font-size: 1.1rem;
        color: #FFFFFF;
        transition: transform 180ms ease;
    }

    details[open] summary::after {
        transform: rotate(180deg);
    }

    summary::-webkit-details-marker {
        display: none;
    }
</style>